        "original_id": "6e609331-47f3-531f-9fa3-fe8752d35a11",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Albert Lee Ueltschi, Joe Engle, Marion Carl, Robin Olds\n- Organizations: National Aviation Hall of Fame, United States Air Force, NASA\n- Places: Dayton, Ohio\n- Roles: test pilot, flying ace, astronaut, aeronautical engineer\n- Programs: North American X-15 program\n\nFacts:\n- On July 21, 2001, Albert Lee Ueltschi was enshrined in Dayton, Ohio, as part of the National Aviation Hall of Fame class of 2001.\n- On July 21, 2001, Albert Lee Ueltschi was enshrined alongside test pilot Joe Engle, United States Air Force flying ace Marion Carl, and USAF ace Robin Olds.\n- Joe Engle is an American pilot who served in the United States Air Force.\n- Joe Engle was a test pilot for the North American X-15 program.\n- Joe Engle is an aeronautical engineer and a former NASA astronaut.",
